==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kelH-}}
Recorded since 1647, from {{der|en|ML.|culminatus}}, the past participle of {{m|la|culminare||to crown}}, from {{der|en|la|culmen||peak, the highest point}}, older form {{m|la|columen||top, summit}}, from {{der|en|itc-pro|*kolamen}}, from a {{der|en|ine-pro|-}} base {{m|ine-pro|*kelH-|*kol-, *kelH-|to project, rise; peak, summit, top}}, whence also {{m+|en|hill}} and {{m|en|holm}}.

===Pronunciation===
